From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:24:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backends: ignore the hand that rests on the screen after a
 pen lifts

libinput ignores the touchscreen of a pen while the pen is near it,
but a pen with a short hover range, such as a Wacom AES pen in a 2-in-1,
leaves proximity whenever it lifts between strokes, and a hand that
lands again a moment later counts as a tap on whatever is under it.

Keep a short pen session in the input thread. Touches on the pen's own
screen, the same libinput device group, are judged by where they land
relative to the last point of the pen and by the hand from
com.lantharos.kestrel.pen. For 1.5 seconds after the pen leaves, a
touch in the area the side of the hand covers (from 50 mm behind the
tip to 140 mm ahead of it, 45 mm above to 95 mm below) is dropped, and
one within 20 mm of it is held for up to 150 ms and let through if it
lifts as a tap, drags away or stays still. Until 4.5 seconds, a touch
in that area waits 450 ms and is dropped if the pen comes back in that
time. A contact that lands within 50 mm of one already taken for a palm
is dropped too, and any touch still held when the pen comes back. Held
touches are replayed with their own times when let through. Without a
pen nearby, touches take the same path as before, and the filter costs
a branch.

Upstream-Status: luft-only tuned on recordings of one 2-in-1; wants hardware data from more pens before it is proposed
